{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Mandate the term \"Care Experienced\" in all public sector communications",
        "additional_details": "We feel the term \"care leaver\" implies care has left us, creating a cliff-edge where support ends. As recent reports on deaths of those leaving care tragically show, it truly feels like care abandons us. We believe there needs to be a language shift that doesn't apply a negative narrative to the Care Experienced Young Person.\r\n\r\nLanguage shapes reality. Shifting to \"Care Experienced\" restores dignity, recognises resilience, and tackles the systemic neglect that leaves vulnerable people isolated.\u201d\r\n",
        "background": "We call on the government to mandate the term \"Care Experienced\" across all professional and legal terminology in public sector communications. We feel that \"Care Leaver\" has a negative connotation to it which for many reinforces the feelings that no one cares.",
